# Every route is prerendered to its own HTML file (vite-react-ssg), so there is
# no SPA fallback here on purpose: an unmatched path falls through to 404.html
# and returns a real 404 instead of a 200 that renders the homepage.

# No canonical-host rule here, deliberately. Pages matches the `from` field on
# path only, so a rule written as `https://www.spladestudio.com/* ... 301` never
# matches and silently does nothing — which is what shipped, and why www served
# the whole site at 200 alongside the apex. The www -> apex 301 lives as a
# zone-level Redirect Rule in Cloudflare instead (Rules > Redirect Rules); see
# MARKETING.md. Until then the <Seo> canonical still points every www page at
# its apex twin, so search consolidates correctly either way.
